{
  "dom_id": "step-q96742",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following functions has the codomain $R?$\n\nI. $p:[0,1]\\to R$\n\nII. $q:R\\to R$\n\nIII. $r:[0,1]\\to [0,1]$",
  "worked_solution": "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $[0,1],$ the interval from $0$ to $1$ (including $0$ and $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
